um.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="425679" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/79/425679/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I933be81c90f1b170511e74422b2d7b763100a0ae" commit="2bf74079cfa7219b8ca625ed671383b47827c049" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mmc: core: Optimize case for exactly one erase-group budget  In the (not so unlikely) case that the mmc controller timeout budget is enough for exactly one erase-group, the simplification of allowing one sector has an enormous performance penalty. We optimize this special case by introducing a flag that prohibits erase-group boundary crossing, so that we can allow trimming more than one sector at a time.  Signed-off-by: David Jander &lt;david@protonic.nl&gt; Signed-off-by: Ulf Hansson &lt;ulf.hansson@linaro.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 642c28ab86f7666d2ac62a0dc391b4c3121f1d6e) Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:59206 TEST=Compile on cyan (not toshiba eMMC): Check discard_max_bytes is expected (1536k).  Change-Id: I933be81c90f1b170511e74422b2d7b763100a0ae Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/420972 Commit-Ready: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="420972" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/72/420972/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I873fa